<figure class="portal-stacking-context" aria-labelledby="portal-stacking-caption">
  <header>
    <span class="eyebrow">Why <code>z-index</code> alone fails</span>
    <strong>Numbers compete inside their own stacking context.</strong>
  </header>
  <div class="portal-stacking-context__stage" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="portal-stacking-context__root">Root page stacking context</span>

    <div class="portal-stacking-context__layer portal-stacking-context__layer--portal">
      <span><code>#modal-root</code></span>
      <strong>Modal</strong>
      <b><code>z-index: 3</code></b>
    </div>

    <div class="portal-stacking-context__layer portal-stacking-context__layer--header">
      <span>Site header</span>
      <b><code>z-index: 2</code></b>
    </div>

    <div class="portal-stacking-context__layer portal-stacking-context__layer--card">
      <span>Dashboard card</span>
      <b><code>z-index: 1</code></b>
      <small>Creates its own stacking context</small>
      <div class="portal-stacking-context__trapped-modal">
        <strong>Modal</strong>
        <b><code>z-index: 9999</code></b>
        <span>Still contained here</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="portal-stacking-context__key">
    <span class="portal-stacking-context__swatch portal-stacking-context__swatch--trapped"></span>
    <span>The child modal cannot out-rank its card's parent layer.</span>
    <span class="portal-stacking-context__swatch portal-stacking-context__swatch--portal"></span>
    <span>A portal moves it to a sibling layer where its own <code>z-index</code> can be managed.</span>
  </div>
  <figcaption id="portal-stacking-caption">A portal can escape a problematic stacking context, but it does not remove the need to choose an appropriate layer at the destination.</figcaption>
</figure>

